    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Assistant-Professor--Industrial-Engineering-and-Industrial-Management_F28-006": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Industrial Engineering and Industrial Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Assistant Professor, Industrial Engineering and Industrial Management   Department: Industrial Engineering/Management   College/Division: School Of Engineering   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The Department of Industrial Engineering & Industrial Management in the School of Engineering at Mercer University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin Fall 2027.   We encourage applications from candidates with teaching and research interests in industrial engineering. We are especially interested in candidates with expertise in operations research, artificial intelligence, machine learning, data-driven decision-making, and emerging technologies. To be considered for a tenure-track position, candidates must have a Ph.D. in industrial engineering or closely related fields. Areas of Emphasis : Areas of emphasis should align with the department’s strengths in optimization, simulation, and supply chain, and should include one or more of the following: artificial intelligence, machine learning, data-driven decision-making, financial engineering, and emerging technologies. Position and Department The Department of Industrial Engineering & Industrial Management offers undergraduate and graduate programs that prepare students for careers in industrial Engineering, Industrial Management, and Engineering Management involving, design, improvement, and installation of integrated systems of people, material, information, equipment, and energy. The department of Industrial Engineering & Industrial Management at Mercer University offers the following degrees: Bachelor of Science in Engineering, with a specialization in Industrial Engineering Bachelor of Science in Industrial Management Master of Science in Engineering with an Engineering Management specialization and Master of Science in Technical Management The discipline draws upon specialized knowledge and skills in the mathematical, physical, and social sciences, together with the principles and methods of engineering analysis and design to specify, predict, and evaluate the results to be obtained from such systems. Because of the need for people skills, the Mercer program places a heavy emphasis on working as a team and working on real industrial engineering problems from neighboring communities. The development of skills required to work with and through other people results in many industrial engineers rising through the ranks of management to the top of technical companies. The industrial specialization at Mercer draws upon four foundational areas—management science, the application of mathematical techniques to solve management problems; ergonomics, the study and design of the interaction between humans and machines; manufacturing, the design and development of processes and systems to transform inputs to products; and quality, the application of statistical methods and managerial principles to improve the quality of products and services. This broad base provides industrial specialization students at Mercer with a solid and varied background. Responsibilities ● Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the department’s programs ● Contribute to service and support courses for the School of Engineering ● Teach in face-to-face, hybrid, and online environments as needed ● Maintain an active agenda of scholarship, creative activity, and/or professionally engaged work ● Contribute to curriculum development and revision in areas such as optimization, systems engineering, artificial intelligence, machine learning, data-driven decision-making, and emerging technologies ● Advise and mentor students ● Support student engagement in applied, research, and professional development opportunities ● Participate in departmental, school, and university service, including assessment and committee work ● Contribute to a team-oriented academic culture Faculty in the department typically teach three courses each semester. Graduate teaching will include online delivery using university-supported platforms and tools. The department’s laboratories, including computer, human factors, and manufacturing labs, support teaching, student collaboration, and faculty-student research and applied project experiences. Required Qualifications: A PhD in industrial engineering or a closely related field from an accredited institution is required by the time of appointment. Additionally, candidates should also have: ● Evidence of strong potential for excellence in teaching ● Expertise in one or more of the areas listed above ● Ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate level ● Ability to teach graduate students, including in online or technology-supported environments ● Ability to work collaboratively in a collegial department ● Familiarity with current and emerging professional tools, practices, and technologies relevant to the field ● An interest in engaging contemporary developments in optimization, systems engineering, and emerging technologies   Application Materials Applicants should submit: ● A cover letter ● Curriculum vitae ● A statement in teaching and research interests (candidates are encouraged to mention existing courses they are qualified to offer, and courses they are interested in developing). ● A list of references with current contact information (at least three) Submission of teaching portfolio and evaluations is optional but encouraged. Additional materials may be requested from finalists, including unofficial transcripts, teaching materials, and/or samples of scholarly or professional work. Official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Selection of the final candidate is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Faculty Engineering   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Atlanta-GA--30341/Admissions-Counselor_27-142": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Admissions Counselor   Department: Admissions   College/Division: General University   Primary Job Posting Location: Atlanta, GA 30341 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University is searching for an Admissions Counselor on the Atlanta, Georgia campus.   Responsibilities : The Admissions Counselor is responsible for the recruitment and admissions of working adult students into undergraduate programs offered by College of Professional Advancement for the Atlanta Campus and Distance Learning as well as Tift College of Education, and Stetson-Hatcher School of Business.  Primary responsibilities include, but are not limited to, recruitment travel, inquiry development, student interviewing, professional presentations, and correspondence. Reporting to the Director of Undergraduate Admissions, RAC, this position works regularly with the Marketing and Communications team for ATL/RAC, all Academic Program Directors, as well as staff members engaged in admissions, alumni and development, and career service functions.   Duties include: Manage the recruitment of qualified students by participating, as needed, through feeder institution visits and presentations, general college fairs, corporate visits, open houses, Chamber events, etc. Ability to understand the specific needs of working adult students.  Planning, organizing and management skills.  Knows how to use Microsoft Office products to maintain accurate prospect management.  Polished presentation/public speaking skills, fine-tuned organization, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills. Ability to conduct interviews and presentations to prospective students and their families.  Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written abilities that positively reflect upon Mercer University with diverse populations, which are vital to the success of this position. Ability to meet and exceed set goals. Availability to travel to event locations (sometimes driving long distances requiring overnight stays) during early morning, evening, and weekend hours as needed. Capability to load and transport admissions materials, displays, and other equipment weighing up to 50 pounds.   Qualifications : A bachelor's degree (preferably in business, marketing, leadership, counseling or education) from an accredited college/university is required. Candidates who have prior experience in admissions/recruitment or a similar sales oriented role preferred. Candidates should have knowledge of Microsoft Office applications for letters, mailings, etc.   Candidates must have a valid driver's license.   Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History   Required Document Attachments: - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Student Operations Exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
