    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Atlanta-GA--30341/Executive-Assistant-to-the-Dean_27-135": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to the Dean",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Executive Assistant to the Dean   Department: Dean's Office, College of Pharmacy   College/Division: College Of Pharmacy   Primary Job Posting Location: Atlanta, GA 30341 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University's College of Pharmacy is searching for an Executive Assistant to the Dean on the Atlanta, Georgia campus.   Responsibilities : The Executive Assistant to the Dean provides high-level administrative support to the Dean and the Dean’s Office, ensuring efficient operations and effective communication within the College and across the University. This position works independently under general to indirect supervision and serves as a key liaison between internal and external stakeholders. Responsibilities include managing schedules, coordinating meetings and events, handling confidential information, and other duties as assigned. Duties include: Executive Support: - Manage the Dean’s calendar, schedule meetings, and coordinate travel arrangements. - Prepare and edit correspondence and reports. Office Operations: - Oversee day-to-day operations of the Dean’s Office, including supervising student workers and managing office supplies. - Serve as the primary point of contact for inquiries and communications. Event and Meeting Coordination: - Organize and support College meetings, committees, and special events. - Coordinate logistics, prepare agendas, and record minutes. Records, Reporting, and Data Management: - Maintain accurate records and ensure compliance with University policies. - Compile and analyze data for reports, including annual reports and accreditation documentation. - Maintain databases and ensure data integrity. Communication and Liaison: - Interface with faculty, staff, students, and external partners professionally and effectively. Qualifications : A bachelor's degree from an accredited college/university and one year of prior administrative support experience is required. In lieu of education, equivalent directly relevant experience, preferably as an administrative or executive assistant, will be considered. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities : Knowledge of scheduling, record-keeping, and administrative workflows. Familiarity with expense tracking, procurement, and basic financial reporting. Awareness of FERPA regulations and institutional confidentiality standards. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, calendar management systems, and virtual meeting platforms. Ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, and complex schedules efficiently. Strong written and verbal communication for drafting correspondence and reports. Skilled at anticipating needs, resolving scheduling conflicts, and handling unexpected issues. Ability to plan and execute meetings, conferences, and special events. Competence in data entry, document formatting, and using collaboration tools (e.g., Teams, Zoom). Ability to handle sensitive information with confidentiality and professionalism. Capacity to work in a fast-paced environment and adjust to changing priorities. Ability to build positive relationships with faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Working knowledge of software systems (e.g., Workday, etc.). Excellent attention to detail, ensuring accuracy in documents, schedules, communication, etc. Ability to work collaboratively. Ability to compile, analyze, and present data accurately. Ability to work with minimal supervision and make sound administrative decisions.   Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History Document Attachments : - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5   Job Family: Staff Clerical Non-exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Valdosta-GA-31602/Clerkship-Coordinator_27-134": {
      "title": "Clerkship Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Clerkship Coordinator   Department: Academic Affairs, School of Medicine   College/Division: School Of Medicine   Primary Job Posting Location: Valdosta, GA 31602 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University is searching for a Clerkship Coordinator at our clinical campus in Valdosta, GA.   Responsibilities : The Clerkship Coordinator manages the 3rd and 4th year programs at our clinical campus in Valdosta, GA, including but not limited to the South Georgia Medical Center (SGMC), to ensure effective service to the students and administrative support for the clinical faculty. Primarily, this position shall coordinate the clinical education program for third year medical students. These duties include but are not limited to: coordination of student schedules; scheduling and proctoring of all third year NBME exams; collection/distribution/statistical reports of student grades to: students, appropriate faculty, and necessary committees; orientation/hospital–specific training for students; makes arrangements/verifies records for visiting students; and point of contact for students and clinical faculty with MUSM. This position will contribute to the Clerkship Manuals in written and web-based formats. This position will serve as the ex-officio member of the Clerkship Directors Sub-Committee of the Curriculum and Instruction Committee and maintain all records for these committees in coordination with other campuses.  This position acts as liaison between MUSM and South Georgia Medical Center, medical schools, hospitals, and physician offices. This position will supervise maintenance of the student lounge and facilities at the hospital and work with Year 3 program Director for third year curriculum and curriculum support concerns. This position will also assist with content input and management in the learning management system and with the master grade reporting in One45 and Excel. This position will serve as the Valdosta clinical site proctor for internal program exams as well as NBME exams. This position manages and promotes relationships with administrators, faculty, and staff at SGMC Medical Center and other Valdosta clinical sites, manages credentialing, and serves as the point of contact for students and clinical faculty for MUSM. This position will be based at South Georgia Medical Center and required to travel to additional off-site clinics and facilities as an essential part of the job. This position will also provide remote support for the third and fourth year programs on other MUSM campuses as needed.   Qualifications: Two years of college coursework and two years of administrative support experience are required. In lieu of education, equivalent directly related experience will be considered. Candidates must have a valid driver's license as this position requires some travel. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities : Serve as a facilitator, resource, and contact person for students, faculty, and staff in the 3rd and 4th-year programs and in all of the specific clerkships. This includes but is not limited to the orientation of students, overseeing the proctoring of NBME exams, and overseeing OSCEs.  Must forge and maintain strong working relationships with Academic Affairs and applicable university committees, by assisting and supporting clerkship staff and faculty across all campuses.  Advanced Excel skills to create and manage various academic and curricular databases.  Capable of organizing and prioritizing workloads to meet deadlines under high pressure.  Capable of learning, instructing, and managing a variety of software platforms and programs (for example, One45, Canvas, ExamSoft, etc.) for the delivery and evaluation of the curriculum and the assessment of students.  Ability to maintain confidentiality of all academic records and ensure this confidentiality even when communicating with students, faculty, and administration. Must exhibit ethical, reliable, and dependable behavior, ability to maintain constructive interpersonal relationships, ability to use judgment to set priorities, teamwork attitude, flexibility, adaptability, and ability to work independently to prioritize/complete tasks.  Ability to multi-task, troubleshoot, and problem-solve. Must have proficiency in Microsoft Office programs, particularly Word and Excel.  Ability communicate (verbal and written) with many organizations internal and external to the university.   Must be detail oriented and highly organized to complete projects for successful outcome.   Background Check Contingencies : - Criminal History Document Attachments : - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Clerical Non-exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Columbus-GA--31901/Faculty--Bioethics-and-Professionalism_F27-065": {
      "title": "Faculty, Bioethics and Professionalism",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Faculty, Bioethics and Professionalism   Department: Bioethics & Medical Humanities   College/Division: School Of Medicine   Primary Job Posting Location: Columbus, GA 31901 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University School of Medicine (MUSM) is seeking a highly qualified educator with broad training and demonstrated experience or enthusiasm for teaching in a medical school curriculum. This position is a tenure track, 12-month appointment on the Columbus, Georgia campus. Additional duties will be required/assigned during the summer. The departmental assignment will be based on degree type and experience.   Responsibilities : The Mercer University School of Medicine has three four year- medical school campuses located in Macon, Georgia: Savannah, Georgia; and Columbus Georgia. The candidate for this position will be based primarily in Columbus though there is an expectation that all bioethics and professionalism faculty will teach on all three campuses both virtually and physically. The selected candidate will work closely with the Chair of the Department of Bioethics and Medical Humanities (Brian H. Childs, PhD—for inquires email childs_bh@mercer.edu ) and the other faculty in the department in creating an integrated ethics and humanities curriculum in both the pre-clinical and clerkship years. Faculty are engaged in a variety of pedagogical modes including Team Based Learning and Problem Based Learning. In addition, the selected candidate will be involved in special programs such as faculty development in ethics education, teaching and grand rounds in our affiliated medical centers, sponsoring student projects and research in bioethics and the medical humanities, as well as faculty committee participation. The department also sponsors a four-year certificate program in bioethics and medical humanities which is open to select students beginning in the second semester of the first pre-clinical year. Qualifications: Candidates must: Hold a terminal degree (PhD, JD, DBe, MD, DO or Equivalent) from an accredited college/university in an appropriate discipline. Demonstrated Training in Ethics Consultation A Commitment to the Mission of Mercer University School of Medicine              Excellent Writing and Communication Skills Research and Teaching in the Medical Humanities Preferred Qualifications: Experience in the Care of the Rural and Underserved A Record of Scholarship and Teaching in Undergraduate Medical Education Certification as a Clinical Ethics Consultant (HEC-C) The ideal candidate will have: Experience independently developing learning resources, independently develop and facilitate large group interactive learning sessions, develop items for assessment of student learning; Experience as a tutor/facilitator of small group interdisciplinary case-based learning sessions in a clinically oriented medical curriculum. Faculty members are expected to participate broadly across the curricula in both the medical and graduate programs, engage in scholarship in areas of Bioethics and Medical Humanities, which includes responsibilities for the four year certificate program in bioethics and medical humanities, as well as interdisciplinary work with the law school, nursing school, pharmacy school and the school of theology. Additional Information The Doctor of Medicine curriculum has been organized and designed to support the mission of the school to train physicians to meet the healthcare needs of rural and other underserved areas of Georgia. The curriculum is patient-centered, providing early application of medical and clinical knowledge in a variety of classroom and clinical venues. The program fosters the development of independent, life-long learning. In addition to the Doctor of Medicine program, the medical school also offers the following degrees: a PhD in Biomedical Sciences; a Master’s in Biomedical Sciences; a Doctor of Philosophy in Rural Healthcare Sciences; and a Master’s in Family Therapy. For over thirty years, MUSM has focused on training medical students to fulfill MUSM’s mission of preparing healthcare professionals to meet the primary care and health care needs of rural and underserved Georgia residents and communities. Emphasizing interactive and problem-based teaching strategies, our student-centered faculty provides a conceptual and practical foundation that equips graduates to be discerning consumers and innovative producers of knowledge across a variety of medical and community settings, as well as academic institutions. Through teaching, scholarship, and service, students and faculty work closely to have local, regional, national, and international impact.   Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History   Required Document Attachments: - CV - Cover letter - explaining teaching philosophy, the candidate's approach to clinical consultation, and their commitment to the rural and underserved population - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Faculty Medicine   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Atlanta-GA--30341/Dean-of-the-Tift-College-of-Education_28-003": {
      "title": "Dean of the Tift College of Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: Please do not click the \"Apply\" button on Mercer University's Careers website. DSG Global has been exclusively retained for this search. To express interest in this role, please submit materials directly to the following: https://talent-profile.dsgco.com/search/v2/23184 Dean of the Tift College of Education Mercer University seeks an accomplished and visionary academic leader to serve as Tift Dean of the College of Education. Mercer University is one of America’s oldest and most distinctive institutions of higher learning, offering rigorous programs that span the undergraduate liberal arts and sciences to doctoral-level degrees. Founded by early 19th-century Baptists, Mercer—while no longer formally denominationally affiliated—remains committed to an educational environment that embraces the historic Baptist principles of intellectual and religious freedom. With about 9,000 students enrolled in 12 Schools and Colleges, on major campuses in Macon and Atlanta, medical school campuses in Macon, Savannah, Columbus, Valdosta, and Carrollton, and at regional academic centers in Henry and Douglas counties, Mercer is ranked among the top tier and best values of national research universities by U.S. News & World Report . For more than 100 years, Mercer University has prepared Georgia's teachers and educational leaders, and today the Tift College of Education carries that legacy forward with a firm commitment to excellence in every aspect of educator preparation. The College prepares educators and educational leaders through innovative, student-centered programs that emphasize academic excellence, hands-on learning, and community engagement. Guided by its mission to prepare educators who teach, learn, create, discover, empower, and serve, the College is committed to advancing educational equity while fostering transformative learning experiences for students and the communities they serve Reporting to the Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost, the Dean is responsible for the overall academic quality, strategic direction, financial health, and operational effectiveness of the College of Education. The next Dean will be a seasoned administrator with deep roots in teacher education and educational leadership programs and who brings both scholarly credibility and a demonstrated record of building innovative, equity-oriented, and transformative learning experiences. The next Dean will be a collaborative and transparent communicator who inspires faculty, staff, and students through a shared vision and inclusive leadership. This individual will also build strong partnerships with school systems and community organizations while successfully navigating the evolving landscape of educator preparation and workforce development in Georgia and beyond. The next Dean will have a terminal degree from an accredited institution in a field relevant to the College's academic portfolio and the academic credentials sufficient for the appointment as a tenured full professor within the College. In addition, they will possess significant progressive leadership experience in higher education, with demonstrated responsibility for academic programs, innovation, personnel, and budget. The search committee will begin accepting and reviewing applications immediately and through Fall 2026. Requested application materials include a letter of interest addressing the leadership agenda and a curriculum vitae/resumé.  Although applications will be accepted until a Dean is selected, for best consideration, all candidates should submit their materials as soon as possible. All materials will be received in confidence. DSG Storbeck has been exclusively retained for this engagement, which is being led by Dr. Thomas Fitch, Managing Director, and Ms. Amanda Bennett, Managing Associate, who can be contacted at MercerEducationDean@dsgco.com . For a full position leadership profile, please click here: https://www.dsgco.com/search/23184-mercer-dean-education/ . To express interest in this role, please submit materials directly to the following: https://talent-profile.dsgco.com/search/v2/23184 .  This is a full-time position that will be based on-site in either Atlanta or Macon, Georgia, with travel to all locations within the state. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and includes a generous benefits package.   EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Human-Centered-Information-Design---Technology_F28-003": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Human-Centered Information Design & Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor, Human-Centered Information Design & Technology   Department: Human-Centered Information Design and Technology   College/Division: School Of Engineering   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The Department of Human-Centered Information Design & Technology in the School of Engineering at Mercer University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, to begin Fall 2027.   We seek a colleague whose teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience reflect the evolving landscape of human-centered, technical, and professional communication in contemporary workplaces. We are particularly interested in candidates whose expertise engages the creation, evaluation, management, and governance of information in complex, technology-mediated, digital, and AI-supported environments. Areas of Emphasis Areas of emphasis should align with the department’s strengths in technical communication, user experience, and artificial intelligence and may include one or more of the following: Accessibility and inclusive design Artificial intelligence and emerging communication technologies Collaborative workflows and project management Content strategy and User experience (UX) Human-computer interaction (HCI) and/or human-robot interaction (HRI) Information design and digital content practices Instructional design and learning experience design International and intercultural communication Technical and professional communication in high-tech environments Technical writing and editing Web design, development, and docs as code Position and Department The Department of Human-Centered Information Design & Technology offers undergraduate and graduate programs that prepare students for careers in technical, professional, digital, and user-centered communication. Located within the School of Engineering, the department provides a distinctive interdisciplinary environment at the intersection of communication, design, technology, and applied problem-solving. The department offers bachelor’s and master’s degree programs, as well as minors in technical communication, user experience, and artificial intelligence, and it provides service courses that support students across the School of Engineering. Faculty also contribute to a two-course sequence in professional and technical communication required for all engineering students. We seek a faculty member who will contribute to a collaborative, collegial, and innovative department and help shape curricula for rapidly changing professional and technological contexts. Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the department’s programs Contribute to service and support courses for the School of Engineering Teach in face-to-face, hybrid, and online environments as needed Maintain an active agenda of scholarship, creative activity, and/or professionally engaged work appropriate to rank Contribute to curriculum development and revision in areas such as AI, UX, accessibility, content strategy, and digital communication Advise and mentor students Support student engagement in applied, research, and professional development opportunities Participate in departmental, school, and university service, including assessment and committee work Contribute to a team-oriented academic culture Faculty in the department typically teach three courses each semester. Graduate teaching will include online delivery using university-supported platforms and tools. The department’s laboratories, including usability and digital media labs, support teaching, student collaboration, and faculty-student research and applied project experiences. Required Qualifications A PhD in technical communication, professional communication, rhetoric, human-centered design, information design, UX, HCI, instructional design, or a closely related field from an accredited institution is required by the time of appointment. Additionally, candidates should also have: Evidence of or strong potential for excellence in teaching Expertise in one or more of the areas listed above Ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate level Ability to teach graduate students, including in online or technology-supported environments Ability to work collaboratively in a collegial department Familiarity with current and emerging professional tools, practices, and technologies relevant to the field An interest in engaging contemporary developments in AI and related communication technologies Preferred Qualifications A record of scholarly, professional, or applied work that demonstrates clear engagement with contemporary communication practice Industry or other professional experience in technical, professional, digital, UX, or content-focused communication settings Experience with accessibility standards, content systems, web technologies, technical editing, or AI-supported communication practices Experience in curriculum innovation, interdisciplinary collaboration, or program development   About Mercer and HID Mercer University is one of the few institutions with technical and professional communication offerings situated within a School of Engineering. This setting creates distinctive opportunities for interdisciplinary teaching, applied collaboration, and innovative program development. The department values human-centered approaches to communication and technology and is committed to preparing students for leadership in contemporary workplaces. Application Materials Applicants should submit: A cover letter Curriculum vitae A list of references with current contact information Additional materials may be requested from finalists, including unofficial transcripts, teaching materials, and/or samples of scholarly or professional work. Official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Selection of the final candidate is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check.   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Faculty Engineering   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Atlanta-GA--30341/Dean-of-the-College-of-Health-Professions_28-002": {
      "title": "Dean of the College of Health Professions",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: Please do not click the \"Apply\" button on Mercer University's Careers website. DSG Global has been exclusively retained for this search. To express interest in this role, please submit materials directly to the following: https://talent-profile.dsgco.com/search/v2/23183 Dean of the College of Health Professions Mercer University seeks an accomplished and visionary academic leader to serve as Dean of the College of Health Professions (CHP). This individual will need to understand the evolving landscape of healthcare workforce development while advancing the CHP’s position as a regional and national leader in preparing practice-ready, ethically grounded health professionals. Mercer University is one of America’s oldest and most distinctive institutions of higher learning, offering rigorous programs that span the undergraduate liberal arts and sciences to doctoral-level degrees. Founded by early 19th-century Baptists, Mercer—while no longer formally denominationally affiliated—remains committed to an educational environment that embraces the historic Baptist principles of intellectual and religious freedom. With about 9,000 students enrolled in 12 schools and colleges, on major campuses in Macon and Atlanta, medical school campuses in Macon, Savannah, Columbus, Valdosta, and Carrollton, and at regional academic centers in Henry and Douglas counties, Mercer is ranked among the top tier and best values of national research universities by U.S. News & World Report . Established in 2013, The College of Health Professions (CHP) is one of Mercer's professional schools and reflects the University's broader commitment to preparing graduates for meaningful careers in service to others. The College offers programs designed to develop skilled, ethical, and compassionate health professionals who are prepared to meet the evolving demands of the healthcare environment. CHP prepares students to improve the health and quality of life of individuals and society through excellence in teaching, research, and service. Reporting to the Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost, the Dean is responsible for the overall academic quality, strategic direction, financial health, and operational effectiveness of the College of Health Professions. The next Dean understands the evolving landscape of healthcare workforce development and can position the CHP as a regional and national leader in preparing practice-ready, ethically grounded health professionals. They are a collaborative, transparent communicator who earns the trust of faculty, staff, students, clinical partners, and University leadership. The next Dean will have a terminal degree from an accredited institution in a field relevant to the College's academic portfolio and the academic credentials sufficient for the appointment as a tenured full professor within one of the College’s departments. In addition, they will possess significant progressive leadership experience in higher education, with demonstrated responsibility for academic programs, innovation, personnel, and budget. The search committee will begin accepting and reviewing applications immediately and through Fall 2026. Requested application materials include a letter of interest addressing the leadership agenda and a curriculum vitae/resumé.  Although applications will be accepted until a Dean is selected, for best consideration, all candidates should submit their materials as soon as possible. All materials will be received in confidence. DSG Global has been exclusively retained for this engagement, which is being led by Dr. Thomas Fitch, Managing Director, and Ms. Amanda Bennett, Managing Associate, who can be contacted at: MercerDeanHealthProfessions@dsgco.com . For a full position leadership profile, please click here: https://dsgco.com/search/ 23183-mercer-dean-health-professions To express interest in this role, please submit materials directly to the following: https://talent-profile.dsgco.com/search/v2/23183 This is a full-time position that will be based on-site in Atlanta, Georgia, with travel to Macon, Georgia. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and includes a generous benefits package. EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Dean-of-the-College-of-Professional-Advancement_28-001": {
      "title": "Dean of the College of Professional Advancement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: Please do not click the \"Apply\" button on Mercer University's Careers website. DSG Global has been exclusively retained for this search. To express interest in this role, please submit materials directly to the following: https://talent-profile.dsgco.com/search/v2/23182 Dean of the College of Professional Advancement Mercer University seeks an accomplished and visionary academic leader to serve as Dean of the College of Professional Advancement (CoPA), an innovative unit dedicated to expanding access to higher education for working adults, non-traditional learners, and professionals seeking to advance their careers. Mercer University is one of America’s oldest and most distinctive institutions of higher learning, offering rigorous programs that span the undergraduate liberal arts and sciences to doctoral-level degrees. Founded by early 19th-century Baptists, Mercer—while no longer formally denominationally affiliated—remains committed to an educational environment that embraces the historic Baptist principles of intellectual and religious freedom. With about 9,000 students enrolled in 12 schools and colleges, on major campuses in Macon and Atlanta, medical school campuses in Macon, Savannah, Columbus, Valdosta, and Carrollton, and at regional academic centers in Henry and Douglas counties, Mercer is ranked among the top tier and best values of national research universities by U.S. News & World Report . The College of Professional Advancement represents one of Mercer’s most distinctive academic units, designed specifically to serve adult learners, working professionals, and students whose educational journeys do not follow a traditional path. The College balances the study of liberal arts with a career-focused education to help students achieve their professional goals. As of 2026, there are 1,200 students enrolled in undergraduate, graduate, professional, and workforce development certificate programs. Reporting to the Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost, the Dean is responsible for the overall academic quality, strategic direction, financial health, and operational effectiveness of the College of Professional Advancement. They will be a seasoned administrator who combines deep respect for the mission of professional and continuing education with the entrepreneurial drive to grow programs, forge community and industry partnerships, and position the College as a regional and national leader in adult learning. They understand the unique needs of non-traditional students, including the importance of flexible delivery, applied curriculum, and meaningful credentialing, and they translate that understanding into strategic program development and student success. The next Dean will have a terminal degree from an accredited institution in a field relevant to the College's academic portfolio and the academic credentials sufficient for the appointment as a tenured full professor within one of the College’s departments. In addition, they will possess significant progressive leadership experience in higher education, with demonstrated responsibility for academic programs, innovation, personnel, and budget. The search committee will begin accepting and reviewing applications immediately and through Fall 2026. Requested application materials include a letter of interest addressing the leadership agenda and a curriculum vitae/resumé.  Although applications will be accepted until a Dean is selected, for best consideration, all candidates should submit their materials as soon as possible. All materials will be received in confidence. DSG Global has been exclusively retained for this engagement, which is being led by Dr. Thomas Fitch, Managing Director, and Ms. Amanda Bennett, Managing Associate, who can be contacted at: MercerDeanProfessionalAdvancement@dsgco.com . For a full position leadership profile, please click here: https://dsgco.com/search/ 23182-mercer-dean-professional-advancement To express interest in this role, please submit materials directly to the following: https://talent-profile.dsgco.com/search/v2/23182 . This is a full-time position that will be based on-site in either Atlanta or Macon, Georgia. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and includes a generous benefits package. EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Swainsboro-GA-30401/Case-Manager_27-131": {
      "title": "Case Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Case Manager   Department: Community Medicine   College/Division: School Of Medicine   Primary Job Posting Location: Swainsboro, GA 30401 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Remote Worker Job Details: The School of Medicine is searching for an Case Manager who resides in the 10 county South Georgia Healthy Start Service area (Appling, Bulloch, Candler, Emanuel, Evans, Jefferson, Jenkins, Screven, Tattnall, Toombs).   Responsibilities : Case Managers will assist with the execution of South Georgia Healthy Start's (SGHS) daily activities to support women, infants, and families in rural South Georgia.  Case Managers will be responsible for recruiting, enrolling, assessing, and retaining participants; providing care navigation and social services enrollment assistance; performing routine check-ins with participants; delivering evidence-based curricula and health education; conducting parenting education classes;  and actively engaging community partners within the SGHS assigned service region.   Case Managers will be expected to participate in professional development and trainings as applicable and may be assigned to lead committees or initiatives within the SGHS program. Qualifications : Bachelor’s and two years of relevant experience, which could include case management, patient navigation, health education, community engagement, survey research, interventionist work, or doula/birthworker experience. In lieu of a bachelor's degree, an equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered.  Valid current driver's license is required. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities : Exceptional interpersonal skills. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to learn and utilize cloud-based case management systems. Ability to travel regularly within the 10-county SGHS project area, as well as to travel occasionally to meetings, trainings, and events throughout the state and in other states.   Background Check Contingencies : - Criminal History Check Document Attachments : - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information Externally Funded : This position is contingent on external funding and the length of employment in this position is dependent on continuation of these funds.   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Administrative Operations Non-exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
