      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nPart time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it, so please review for accuracy prior to submission . Job Title: Adjunct Faculty/PRN Professionals - College of Education   Department: Dean's Office, College of Education   College/Division: College Of Education   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Atlanta, GA 30341, McDonough, GA 30253 Job Details: The College of Education at Mercer University invites applications for inclusion in its Adjunct Faculty/PRN Professionals Applicant Pool.   Job Summary The College of Education seeks qualified professionals and educators who are interested in contributing to the preparation of our students through teaching, mentoring, and academic engagement. Adjunct faculty members and PRN professionals are appointed on a semester-by-semester basis to provide instruction or other learning opportunities in undergraduate, graduate, and/or professional programs. This posting is intended to establish and maintain a pool of qualified candidates for potential teaching and professional opportunities. Applications will be reviewed by the appropriate academic units as instructional needs arise. Submission of an application does not guarantee employment or an offer of a teaching assignment. Mercer University welcomes applications from both individuals who have been identified through academic unit recruitment efforts and qualified external candidates interested in future instructional opportunities. Qualifications Minimum qualifications vary by discipline and academic program. Applicants should possess: A master's degree or higher in the discipline or a closely related field, where appropriate Relevant professional, academic, clinical, or industry experience Additional qualifications may be required to meet accreditation, licensure, or program-specific standards.   Applicants should submit: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Any additional materials required by the specific school or college This is a continuous posting used to develop and maintain a pool of Adjunct Faculty/PRN Professional candidates. Applications may remain active for consideration for future instructional opportunities. Assignments are contingent upon departmental needs, budget availability, enrollment, and approval by the appropriate academic administrators. For additional information or questions, please contact the Dean's Office or visit: https://education.mercer.edu/   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. Job Family: Faculty Adjunct, Staff Other Exempt PAP   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
