    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Columbus-GA--31901/Vivarium-and-Research-Lab-Manager_27-117": {
      "title": "Vivarium and Research Lab Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Vivarium and Research Lab Manager   Department: Biomedical Sciences   College/Division: School Of Medicine   Primary Job Posting Location: Columbus, GA 31901 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University School of Medicine is seeking a highly qualified Vivarium and Research Lab Manager on the Columbus, GA campus.   Responsibilities : As Vivarium and Research Lab Manager, the incumbent will be responsible for managing and performing all activities within the animal vivarium on the Columbus campus to include all aspects of animal husbandry and care. This position will be responsible for all reporting requirements associated with IACUC, OLAW, and USDA oversight. This position will insure creation, maintenance of, and adherence to standard operating procedures and protocols. The candidate will have access to a veterinarian and other facility managers as needed. As Research Lab Manager the incumbent will work with the Chair or Vice-Chair of the department to perform duties related to managing and maintaining the research laboratory facilities on the Columbus campus of MUSM. The Laboratory Manager will be responsible for maintaining as well as ensuring proper and safe use of departmental equipment. In consultation with the Department Chair or Vice-Chair, the laboratory manager will help to monitor proper adherence to departmental policies regarding conducting research, use of resources, handling and disposal of research materials. In addition, the laboratory manager will monitor departmental usage of laboratory supplies, assist in ordering supplies and advising on current and future equipment needs. Qualifications : A bachelor's degree in biomedical sciences or a related field from an accredited institution and five years of prior laboratory experience which must include work with animals. Candidates with a master's degree and two years of the same experience will also be considered. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities : Must know how to use Microsoft Word and Excel to prepare various reports. Must be able to learn and apply basic principles and practices of laboratory animal care and facility maintenance. Must be able to keep written records of animal health, daily tasks, and facility conditions. Must be able to learn and abide by the IACUC, OLAW, and USDA regulations as they apply to a laboratory animal vivarium. Must be able to write and follow standard operating procedures and protocols for the vivarium and research laboratory. Must be able to work with disinfectants, germicides, and cleaning agents commonly used in the animal vivarium. Must be able to work on rotating weekends and holidays in the animal vivarium. Must learn how to troubleshoot and maintain vivarium and research laboratory equipment.   Background Check Contingencies : - Criminal History Document Attachments : - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Student Operations Exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Executive-Assistant-to-the-Dean_27-113": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to the Dean",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Executive Assistant to the Dean   Department: Dean's Office, School of Business   College/Division: School Of Business   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The School of Business is searching for an Executive Assistant to the Dean on the Macon, Georgia campus.   Responsibilities : The Executive Assistant will assist the Dean’s Office and Program Directors with a large variety of duties, especially web- and technology-based.  Technology-related duties include extensive knowledge of the Microsoft Office suite, learning management systems, student academic record systems, and Workday.  This position must provide the Dean’s Office with the necessary information to effectively lead the School of Business and carry out its day-to-day operations in Macon.  The Executive Assistant must be able to assume full responsibility, frequently working independently, to see assigned duties and projects through to completion in an efficient and effective way with little or no direct supervision.  Requiring excellent written and oral communication skills, this position must have the knowledge and communication skills to work well with the faculty, staff, and students to assure our students the best educational experience possible. The Executive Assistant will also handle accounting, payroll, budgeting, and personnel assistance.   Other duties of this position include staff assignments, arranging meetings and functions, and supervising and hiring student workers and other staff.  This position generally works independently with little or no supervision, and the responsibilities handled are intended to ensure the efficient operation of the School of Business in Macon and all its related degree programs and constituencies. The Executive Assistant will also support the Director of Operations on the Macon Campus, by assisting with AACSB reports, faculty evaluation, supplies and office management, recruiting and supervising student workers, handling special events such as faculty meetings and graduation reception, and serving as a liaison to the Macon campus faculty. Qualifications : A bachelor's degree from an accredited college/university and one year of prior administrative support experience is required. In lieu of education, equivalent directly relevant experience will be considered. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Ability to work independently, demonstrating self-reliance and initiative.   Ability to expedite office workload without supervision, exercise judgment in prioritizing tasks and respond professionally and efficiently to new situations that have not been previously encountered while managing heavy workload. Ability to quickly learn how Stetson-Hatcher School of Business (SHSB) functions in order to work with maximum efficiency and effectiveness and quickly assimilate knowledge to implement and give understandable interpretations of SHSB policies. Self-starter with progressive administrative experience with the ability to adapt quickly and maintain attention to detail while working under pressure and dealing with interruptions. Experience with or ability to learn basic HR processes to help facilitate the recruiting of student workers and adjunct faculty and performance evaluations of staff and faculty, enabling this person to provide greater support to the Dean, Associate Dean, and/or Director of Operations. Strong organizational skills to help run the office efficiently and effectively. Initiative to prioritize, begin, and complete projects within a given time frame and without direct supervision. Ability to quickly learn the university’s policies to work well with other departments/schools. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to communicate effectively in both written and verbal forms.   Must have a demonstrated capability of handling sensitive and confidential data/information.   Selection of the final candidate is contingent on a successful criminal history check. Document Attachments: - Resume - Cover letter - List of references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Clerical Non-exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Jekyll-Island-GA--31527/Primary-Care-Physician--Family-or-Internal-Medicine_27-108": {
      "title": "Primary Care Physician, Family or Internal Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Primary Care Physician, Family or Internal Medicine   Department: Family Medicine   College/Division: School Of Medicine   Primary Job Posting Location: Jekyll Island, GA 31527 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The Mercer University School of Medicine is seeking a physician to perform full time in a clinical practice at one of the Mercer Medicine rural clinic locations in Jekyll Island, Georgia. Clinical practice and pre-clinical training is through Mercer Medicine. The mission of the school is to train physicians and other healthcare professionals in primary care and service to rural and underserved populations in Georgia.   This position is expected to maintain a financially viable clinical practice at our Mercer Medicine rural clinic in Jekyll Island, GA. This is a 12-month professional staff position that will report to the Director of the Rural Clinics. Candidates must: Hold an M.D. degree and be board certified in Family Medicine or Internal Medicine, and be licensed to practice medicine in the state of Georgia. The candidate must also demonstrate strong experience in working in interdisciplinary healthcare education and clinical settings. The ideal candidate will have: Experience in a health-related clinical area is desirable. Experience in both an inpatient and outpatient basis is desirable Ability to work well with others in an academic setting Excellent written and verbal communication skills Experience presenting and communicating medical concepts to clinical and lay audiences Familiarity and/or experience with medical settings and culture Experience working with stakeholders and communities in rural, medically underserved areas of Georgia   Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History   Required Document Attachments: - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Clinical Services Exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Chair--Biomedical-Sciences_F27-062": {
      "title": "Chair, Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-14\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Chair, Biomedical Sciences   Department: Biomedical Sciences   College/Division: School Of Medicine   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University School of Medicine is searching for a tenure track faculty position for the Chair of the Department of Biomedical Sciences on the Macon campus.   Responsibilities : Mercer University School of Medicine (MUSM) invites applications for the position of Department Chair for the Biomedical Sciences Department on the Macon campus. The Chair leads a growing, multidisciplinary faculty who are active in research and teaching. The Chair will oversee the growth in academic programs, research infrastructure, and external research funding.  Mercer University School of Medicine is a community-based medical school that educates health professionals to provide care in rural, medically underserved areas of Georgia ( http://medicine.mercer.edu ). This is a 12-month, full-time, tenure-track appointment.  Rank to be determined based on the credentials of the selected candidate. Candidates must meet the standards for tenure and rank in the department. Candidates must have a track record of lead author publications in peer-reviewed journals and plans for establishing an independent research program. Should have a strong track record in externally funded research.  Must establish and maintain a vigorous, extramurally funded research program in their area of expertise, and contribute to teaching graduate and/or medical students associated with the Department of Biomedical Sciences. Duties include : Provide leadership and administration of the Department of Biomedical Sciences on all three MUSM campuses; Serve as a liaison to all committees or groups as needed or assure representation from the department of Biomedical Sciences; Support the departmental faculty with emphasis on their responsibilities for the educational and research programs; Participate in on-going readiness for accreditation and ensure that the Department of Biomedical Sciences participates in continuous quality improvement; Teach Biomedical Sciences in both small and large group settings; Manage Biomedical Sciences faculty to include making sure there are adequate faculty designated to teach both large and small groups Participate and collaborate in research activity and with national organizations that maintain and enhance administrative and educational skills in Biomedical Sciences education and administration; Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent degree in a biomedical science from an accredited college/university. Mission-focused leadership experience. A record of excellence in research. A commitment to excellence in medical education. Familiarity and/or experience with rural areas. Desirable Qualifications: Current extramural research funding is highly desirable. Experience in teaching Biomedical Sciences to medical students. Experience in small group, team-based, interdisciplinary teaching, and student evaluation. Administrative experience and the ability to manage department finances, academic, administrative, and personnel matters. Strong interpersonal, communication and organizational skills. Commitment to develop a rural research focus both personally, with other faculty, and students. Familiarity and experience with rural Georgia.   Selection of the final candidate is contingent on a successful background check. Required Document Attachments : - CV - Cover Letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Faculty Medicine   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
