    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Warner-Robins-GA--31088-7810/Chief-Software--Software_26-SW-15-1": {
      "title": "Chief Engineer, Software",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-19\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Chief Engineer, Software   Department: MERC   College/Division: Mercer Engineering Research Center   Primary Job Posting Location: Warner Robins, GA 31088-7810 Job Details: Mercer Engineering Research Center (MERC), a research institute of Mercer University, provides high quality engineering, scientific, and technical support services to both government and private industry customers. MERC is currently recruiting for a Chief Engineer, Software for its Software and Cyber Directorate. The Chief Engineer will be responsible for the execution of all contractual efforts, including design, development, prototyping, production, operation, etc., as applicable. Sets the example for and advises/mentors all technical leads and contract personnel. Performs all duties and responsibilities under the supervision of the respective technical director.   REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: US Citizenship Ability to obtain and maintain a DoD Security Clearance • Undergraduate degree in a relevant engineering field (e.g., Software Engineer, Computer Engineer, Computer Science) from an ABET accredited institution and 13 years of directly related technical experience or • Master’s degree in same and 12 years of directly related technical experience or • Ph.D. and 10 years of directly related technical experience • Experience leading technical teams from a variety of different backgrounds and disciplines. • Extensive experience in the designated industry including but not limited to: aerospace, electrical, software, environmental, biomedical, mechanical, and systems engineering • Knowledge of engineering principles (e.g. analysis, test, and design) • Exceptional organizational and time management skills with an obsessive attention to detail • Able to collaborate and bridge the communication gap between the engineering team, service technicians, business development, operations staff, and clients • Superior budgeting and cost management abilities, assessing estimated costs early in the program and bringing the actual costs within budget. • Able to draft clear and comprehensive reports on assigned contracts, the use and allocation of resources, and the quality of each finished program • Possess technical acumen and the ability to troubleshoot on a variety of programs • Able to perform business development activities to include customer interface, estimating and scheduling, technical proposal development, and follow through • Ability to take a concept from an idea to an actual working model • knowledge of Web applications, cybersecurity, CI-CD, and big data concepts and technologies DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS: • CompTIA Security Plus • ISC^2 CSSLP Final rank will be determined on the qualifications of the selected candidate. Application must include a cover letter and resume. BENEFITS OF WORKING AT MERC MERC is a non-profit research institute of Mercer University, a private university founded in 1833. Established in 1987 in Warner Robins, GA, MERC employs more than 200 engineers, scientists, professors, and support staff, who provide sustainable research solutions to government agencies, the Department of Defense, and commercial customers around the world. Warner Robins and the middle GA area are located 90 miles south of Atlanta and within easy driving distance of both the beach and mountains. The area is known for its Southern-style music, food, and restaurants and has a rich cultural and art presence, along with excellent health care and schools. MERC offers a generous benefits package including health and dental insurance, retirement, tuition reimbursement, vacation/sick leave accrual, and holiday pay.     Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff MERC Exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Atlanta-GA--30341/Coordinator-of-Experiential-Learning_27-031": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Experiential Learning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-19\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Coordinator of Experiential Learning   Department: Physician Assistant Studies   College/Division: College Of Health Professions   Primary Job Posting Location: Atlanta, GA 30341 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University's College of Health Professions is searching for a Coordinator of Experiential Learning for the Physician Assistant Program on the Atlanta campus.   Responsibilities : The Coordinator of Experiential Learning has the responsibility of coordination and oversight for the administrative responsibilities of the clinical year for the Physician Assistant Program in the College of Health Professions at Mercer University.  This position is responsible for coordination clinical practicums with preceptors. The successful candidate will be able to handle multiple higher-level tasks simultaneously, possess excellent time management skills, and work with changing priorities throughout the clinical year.  Exceptional organizational skills are required with excellent attention to detail.  This person must be able to communicate clearly, effectively and correctly in both verbal and written form, as well as exhibit professionalism. They must work extremely well in a team environment yet possess the capacity to work independently. This person will serve as the first-line contact for clinical students and Preceptors for the Physician Assistant Program and must be comfortable speaking directly to physicians, clinical office staff, and working directly with students in a clinical setting. Additionally, some travel will be required. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Proven ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously with strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to prioritize competing demands. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Windows, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Access) to develop presentations, policies, databases, assessment tools, and program materials. Experience with database management, including maintaining contact, rotation, and program data within E*Value systems. Ability to support preceptors in the effective use of EValue software and utilize EVOS for annual clinical scheduling. Working knowledge of university systems, including FRS, R25 room scheduling, OnTime calendar system, and Microsoft Outlook. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion with sensitive program, faculty, and student information. Strong communication and customer service skills, including effective interoffice communication, phone system operation, and mail handling procedures. Ability to build and maintain professional relationships with students, faculty, staff, and healthcare partners. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team-oriented environment. Ability to engage with and recruit healthcare professionals as clinical preceptors. Willingness and ability to travel and interact with members of the healthcare team. Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree in Business, Marketing and Sales, Biology/Sciences, Human Resources, Health Information, or a related degree is required, along with three years of directly relevant experience that could include sales/marketing, recruitment, prior experience in a health sciences-related environment, and/or prior experience in a healthcare environment.   Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History   Required Document Attachments: - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Clerical Non-exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Atlanta-GA--30341/Research-Scientist_27-027": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-04\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Research Scientist   Department: Dean's Office, College of Pharmacy   College/Division: College Of Pharmacy   Primary Job Posting Location: Atlanta, GA 30341 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University College of Pharmacy is searching for a Research Scientist on the Atlanta, Georgia campus.   Responsibilities : The postdoctoral Research Scientist in the Hasan Lab at Mercer University will serve as a senior-level investigator leading independent and collaborative research projects in cardiovascular drug discovery. Projects in the lab are focused on understanding and targeting ion channels and G-protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs) to identify novel therapeutic targets, and develop new drug candidates for hypertension, stroke and cardiometabolic diseases. The incumbent will design and execute studies using a comprehensive and integrative experimental approach that includes pressure myography, Ca2+ imaging, advanced microscopy, flow cytometry, genetic approaches, cell culture, molecular biology, luminescence-based assays, ELISA, Western blotting, enzyme activity assays, immunocytochemistry and immunohistochemistry, biophysical analyses of ligand–receptor interactions, blood pressure analysis, as well as in silico modeling and molecular dynamics simulations. In addition, the postdoctoral Research Scientist will contribute to grant development, assist the PI in manuscript preparation,  and support laboratory operations, ensuring high standards of rigor, reproducibility, and compliance. This position exercises a high degree of scientific independence and contributes to the strategic direction and growth of the research program. Required Qualifications : A PhD in Pharmacology, Physiology, Molecular Biology, or a closely related biomedical discipline and a minimum of three years of postdoctoral experience demonstrating the ability to conduct independent research and contribute to the development and direction of an established research program are required. Preferred Qualifications: Substantial experience in grant and manuscript preparation and publications. Experience contributing to or leading competitive grant applications. Experience with experimental approaches using animal models of disease, including hypertension, stroke, diabetes, and pulmonary hypertension. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Solid knowledge in cardiovascular sciences, metabolic disorders and intracellular signal transduction pathways. Proficiency in experimental techniques relevant to animal models of diseases such as hypertension, diabetes, stroke, and pulmonary hypertension.  Ability to design, execute, and manage independent research projects from conception to publication.  Proven ability to design and lead independent research projects and contribute to competitive grant applications.  Excellent organizational, problem-solving, and leadership skills, with the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Solid knowledge in cardiovascular sciences, metabolic disorders and intracellular signal transduction pathways. Proficiency in experimental techniques relevant to animal models of diseases such as hypertension, stroke, preeclampsia, pulmonary hypertension, and diabetes.  Ability to design, execute, and manage independent research projects from conception to publication.  Proven ability to design and lead independent research projects and contribute to competitive grant applications.  Excellent organizational, problem-solving, and leadership skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research team.    Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History Required Document Attachments: - Resume/CV - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information Externally Funded: This position is contingent on external funding and the length of employment in this position is dependent on continuation of these funds.   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Research and Lab Services Exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Atlanta-GA--30341/Faculty--Clinical-Psychology_F27-029": {
      "title": "Faculty, Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-29\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Faculty, Clinical Psychology   Department: Clinical Psychology   College/Division: College Of Health Professions   Primary Job Posting Location: Atlanta, GA 30341 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The College of Health Professions at Mercer University invites applications for a full-time faculty member for the Doctor of Psychology Program. This position is for a tenure-track faculty in a progressive and innovative department that emphasizes evidence-based treatment, an integrative approach to healthcare, and interaction with our other partner programs (Physical Therapy, Physician Assistant Studies, Public Health, Athletic Training, and Kinesiology). Rank will be determined based on the credentials of the selected candidate.   Responsibilities Responsibilities include doctoral student classroom instruction and evaluation; small group support for clinical training; advisement and mentoring of students; admissions and accreditation activities; committee involvement; and scholarly activities to include publications, grants, presentations, and collaborative projects. Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, clinical training, and student mentorship within a practitioner-scholar model. The ideal candidates also will have a strong research orientation with established or potential for extramural support. As a faculty member at Mercer University, you can expect to be immersed into a community of scholars who are committed to excellence. Qualifications General qualifications include a degree from an APA-accredited PhD or PsyD Clinical Psychology program and completion of an APA-accredited internship. Active, unrestricted license to practice as a clinical psychologist in Georgia or immediate eligibility is required. Prior experience teaching, supervising, and mentoring graduate students is preferred. Preference for this position will be given to someone with expertise and teaching experience in Cognitive Assessment . A background in clinical neuropsychology, with the ability to teach Neuropsychological Assessment and Biological Bases of Behavior , is also desirable. Other areas of expertise within clinical psychology will be considered. Additional Information This position will be a 12-month appointment based at Mercer University’s Cecil B. Day campus in Atlanta, Georgia, conveniently located near all the amenities of the city and situation on over 250 wooded acres. More information can be found at http://www.mercer.edu/ . Questions regarding this position may be directed to Dr. Michelle Robbins, robbins_mm@mercer.edu , 678.547.6225. Interested applicants will need to complete the brief online application and attach a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, description of research agenda, and the names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately.   Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History   Required Document Attachments: - Current CV - Letter of Interest - Statement of Teaching Philosophy - Description of Research Agenda - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Faculty Health Professions   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
