    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Warner-Robins-GA--31088-7810/Senior-Electrical-Engineer_27-EWA-02": {
      "title": "Senior Electrical Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Senior Electrical Engineer   Department: MERC   College/Division: Mercer Engineering Research Center   Primary Job Posting Location: Warner Robins, GA 31088-7810 Job Details: Mercer Engineering Research Center (MERC) is recruiting for a Senior Electrical Engineer to support its Electronic Warfare and Avionics area. This is a full time, on-site position located in Warner Robins, GA.   DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES • Responsible for leading, designing, and performing detailed engineering efforts in the assigned discipline, including but not limited to providing leadership and participating with a technical team in the conduct of the following tasks: Analyzing existing technology applications, processes, and products, taking into consideration costs, life cycle considerations, reliability, maintainability, productivity, and long-term support. Performing intensive technology research & evaluation of a broad array of alternative solutions to improve existing implementations. Defining and implementing advanced technological implementations and evaluations to provide risk reduction & determine production feasibility of improved and alternate technological implementations. Designing, implementing, and achieving operational status of advanced technological and engineering approaches to satisfy customer needs. • Responsible for organizing, conducting, and achieving detailed cross-functional engineering communication, design, evaluation, and implementations providing novel and unique functionality and capability through multi-disciplined engineering applications through: Organizing technical teams of multi-disciplined persons to construct a range of technological implementations and solutions for a problem area. Participation in multidiscipline design teams and process action team efforts. Preparing and presenting design alternatives to a multidiscipline review peer group. Preparing and implementing designs that apply multidiscipline solutions achieving breakthrough performance and unique technological applications. • Responsible for leading technical teams in their technical interface with present and perspective customers through the following activities: Diagnosing existing and perspective customer needs and opportunities through informal and formal interaction to understand present operations and limitations and customer priorities and needs. Leading teams in preparing and presenting detailed program presentations providing technical solutions, cost estimates, and implementation schedules, using information gathered both directly and indirectly to provide customer insight into technological capabilities that could significantly improve operations. Ensuring strong technical communication and understanding through use of terms, design illustrations, and operating paradigms that are common to customer experience. Gathers, tracks, maintains, and provides detailed technical, cost, labor, material, and schedule information on programs to senior managers including cost, schedule, and technical risk assessments at all stages of implementation. Complies with all Executive Director approved MERC-wide policies and procedures. Adheres to approved MERC MSP quality management policies and principles and promotes an attitude of commitment to continuous quality improvement. Ensures thorough familiarity and awareness of all MERC core capabilities and with the MERC current and potential customer base. During all business-related activities, particularly during customer contacts, remains alert for any problem or opportunity that might lead to additional business for any MERC core business area. Whenever possible, use any available opportunity to promote MERC capabilities and interests to customers and potential customers. Submit suggestions for new business opportunities or report identified customer problems or opportunities to the Director of Acquisition Strategy through a Chief Engineer. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS • US Citizenship is required. • Ability to obtain and maintain a DoD Security Clearance. • A Ph.D. in a relevant engineering field (e.g., EE, ME, AE, IE, SW, CE, Computer Science, etc.) from an ABET accredited institution and 3 years of directly related experience; or a Master’s degree in same and 8 years of directly related experience; or an undergraduate degree in same and 9 years of directly related experience. • 3 years of technical lead responsibility. • Additional requirements may be added as appropriate and as specified in the specific Personnel Requisition Form. Final rank will be determined on the qualifications of the selected candidate. BENEFITS OF WORKING AT MERC  MERC is a non-profit applied research operating unit of Mercer University, a private university founded in 1833. Established in 1987 in Warner Robins, GA, MERC employs more than 200 engineers, scientists, professors, and support staff, who provide sustainable research solutions to government agencies, the Department of Defense, and commercial customers around the world. Warner Robins and the middle GA area are located 90 miles south of Atlanta and within easy driving distance of both the beach and mountains. The area is known for its Southern-style music, food, and restaurants and has a rich cultural and art presence, along with excellent health care and schools. MERC offers a generous benefits package including health and dental insurance, retirement, tuition reimbursement, vacation/sick leave accrual, and holiday pay.     Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff MERC Exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice_F28-014": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Assistant Professor of Practice   Department: Journalism & Media Studies   College/Division: College Of Liberal Arts And Sciences   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The Reg Murphy Center for Collaborative Journalism in partnership with Mercer University’s Department of Journalism and Media Studies is seeking applications for a non-tenure track position as an Assistant Professor of Practice.   Responsibilities : This non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Practice position involves teaching journalism courses for the Journalism & Media Studies department, providing service to the University, and staying active professionally with work for the Reg Murphy Center for Collaborative Journalism and other external partners. We are interested in applicants who are practicing or former journalists that can teach courses in data journalism, investigative reporting, and audio reporting for students learning to produce content for print, radio, broadcast, and online news outlets. The candidate will be expected to teach additional courses in the Journalism and Media Studies programs based on their background and expertise. We are most interested in candidates that can teach additional courses on digital and social media, broadcast journalism, public relations, entrepreneurship, and/or community engagement. The candidate will also remain active in a professional capacity by contributing journalistic work to our community news site, The Macon Newsroom, and other partner and professional news organizations. Additional responsibilities for the position include advising and mentoring students and contributing to departmental and university service requirements. Qualifications : A master’s degree in Journalism or related discipline is required, along with at least five years of experience in a professional newsroom or media organization, where the candidate utilized data journalism and/or audio storytelling. Candidates must be able to teach Data Journalism and Audio Journalism courses. Candidates with previous teaching experience, experience in multimedia reporting, and proficiency in editing with Adobe Creative Cloud tools are strongly preferred. Additionally, candidates should have strong storytelling skills, excellent interpersonal and organizational skills, and interest in teaching journalism within a larger liberal arts curriculum. Candidates selected for the first round of interviews will be asked to send unofficial graduate transcripts (redact any personal or private identifying information including, but not limited to: social security number, birthdate, race or gender, before submitting).  Additional Information: Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a dynamic and comprehensive center of undergraduate, graduate and professional education. With more than 9,200 students enrolled in 12 schools and colleges, on major campuses in Macon and Atlanta; medical school sites in Macon, Savannah, Columbus and Valdosta; and at regional academic centers in Henry and Douglas counties, Mercer is ranked among the top tier and best values of national research universities by U.S. News & World Report . The Mercer Health Sciences Center includes the University’s School of Medicine and Colleges of Nursing, Health Professions and Pharmacy. Mercer is affiliated with six teaching hospitals – Atrium Health Navicent The Medical Center and Piedmont Macon Medical Center in Macon; Memorial Health University Medical Center in Savannah; Piedmont Columbus Regional Hospital and St. Francis-Emory Healthcare in Columbus; and SGMC Health in Valdosta. The University also has an educational partnership with Robins Air Force Base in Warner Robins. It operates an academic press and a performing arts center in Macon and an engineering research center in Warner Robins. Mercer Medicine, the clinical faculty practice of the School of Medicine, is based in Macon and operates additional clinics in Sumter, Clay, Putnam, Harris, Taylor and Glynn counties. Mercer is one of only 293 institutions nationwide to shelter a chapter of The Phi Beta Kappa Society, the nation’s most prestigious academic honor society; one of eight institutions to hold membership in the Georgia Research Alliance; and the only private university in Georgia to field an NCAA Division I athletic program. The Reg Murphy Center for Collaborative Journalism incorporates partnerships with the Journalism and Media Studies department as well local media outlets to include Georgia Public Broadcasting, The Macon Melody, and 13WMAZ, The Journalism and Media Studies department has six faculty members and offers a BA in Journalism and a BA in Media Studies as well as a minor in Film Studies.   Candidates should complete the brief online application and attach the following required documents: 1) A Cover Letter  2) Curriculum Vitae  3) A statement of Teaching Philosophy and/or experience  4) Contact information for three professional references  Selection of the final candidate is contingent on a successful criminal background check.   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Faculty Arts   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Assistant-Professor-of-Philosophy_F28-013": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Assistant Professor of Philosophy   Department: Philosophy   College/Division: College Of Liberal Arts And Sciences   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The Department of Philosophy at Mercer University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor.  The anticipated start date is August 1, 2027.   Responsibilities Area of Specialization is “Ethics,” but the term should be broadly construed to include related subfields such as history of moral philosophy, contemporary moral issues, social epistemology, and so forth.  An interest in, and facility with, medical humanities or medical ethics is preferred.  Area of Competence is History of Philosophy / Ideas, in keeping with one of the department’s traditional strengths. Successful candidates will be prepared to teach Introduction to Philosophy, Introduction to Ethics, and Logic.  The typical teaching load at Mercer is 21 credit hours annually on a semester system.  A hire for this position will be expected to teach at least three of those credit hours in either the Great Books Program or in the Integrative Studies program. A hire for this position will have the opportunity (but not the expectation) to work with associated University centers such as the McDonald Center for America’s Founding Principles and the Center for Leadership, Ethics, and Service; and to participate in traditional study abroad programs (e.g., Philosophy and the Arts) as well as global service programs (e.g., Mercer on Mission). Information on Great Books - https://greatbooks.mercer.edu/ Information on Integrative Studies - https://liberalarts.mercer.edu/about/core-curriculum-for-general-education/integrative-curriculum/ Information on the McDonald Center for America’s Founding Principles – https://afp.mercer.edu/ Information on the Center for Leadership, Ethics, and Service - https://lead.mercer.edu/ Information on Study Abroad - https://liberalarts.mercer.edu/academic-departments/international-and-global-studies/study-abroad/ Qualifications A Ph.D. (or equivalent degree) from an accredited college/university in philosophy must be completed by August 1, 2027. ABD candidates will be considered at the rank of Instructor until the Ph.D. has been obtained. About the Department of Philosophy Our department ( https://liberalarts.mercer.edu/academic-departments/philosophy/ ) affirms Mercer University’s position—demonstrated in its many efforts at local, regional, and global outreach—that there is a practical, world-changing benefit to studying the liberal arts and sciences in addition to the benefit of self-development. A traditional strength of the department has been history of philosophy.  We also emphasize practical skill development (e.g., critical thinking and close reading) and the application of moral reasoning to real-world problems. The department offers BA degrees in Philosophy and in Philosophy, Politics, and Economics.   About the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences ( https://liberalarts.mercer.edu/ ) is the cornerstone of Mercer University’s undergraduate presence as well as its oldest and largest academic division. With a deep commitment to liberal education, over 130 full-time faculty members offer nearly 40 academic programs in the arts, humanities, natural sciences, physical sciences, and social sciences. Additionally, the faculty provide the general education of the 3,400 traditional students enrolled in the College and in the other four Macon traditional undergraduate schools (business, education, engineering, and music). The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences is located 80 miles south of Atlanta in Macon (pop. 150,000), a beautiful metropolitan area enjoying an internationally recognized renaissance. Macon boasts historic architecture, a revitalized downtown, a vibrant arts and music scene, a demographically diverse community, and the United States' next national park.   About Mercer University In recent years, Mercer University ( https://www.mercer.edu/ ) students have earned dozens of Goldwater Scholarships, Fulbright Scholarships, NSF Graduate Research Fellowships, Critical Language Scholarships, and other nationally competitive fellowships and scholarships. Mercer is the nation’s top producer of Gilman Scholars among schools with fewer than 5,000 undergraduates. Mercer is also one of only three Georgia universities that both shelter a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa and hold membership in the Georgia Research Alliance. With respect to service, the University has aided the revitalization of local historic neighborhoods, funded rural health clinics throughout the state, and deployed faculty and students to 45 international locales via its global service program, Mercer On Mission. With over 9,100 students enrolled in twelve colleges and with campuses in Macon, Atlanta, Savannah and Columbus, Mercer has an extensive and robust footprint in Georgia.   Background Check Contingencies Criminal History Check Required Document Attachments Interested applicants should complete an online application at https://hr.mercer.edu/jobs/ and attach 1) a letter of interest, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) a one-page teaching statement, and 4) a list of professional references with contact information. Candidates selected for the first round of interviews will be asked to send unofficial graduate transcripts (redact any personal or private identifying information including, but not limited to: social security number, birthdate, race or gender, before submitting). Finalists may be asked for additional materials.  Review of applications will begin immediately.  To ensure full consideration, please submit all materials no later than December 4, 2026.  All correspondence and inquiries should be emailed to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Kevin S. Honeycutt ( honeycutt_ks@mercer.edu )   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Faculty Social Sciences   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Library-Assistant-II_27-153": {
      "title": "Library Assistant II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Library Assistant II   Department: Tarver Library   College/Division: General University   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: Mercer University is searching for a Library Assistant II on the Macon, Georgia campus.   Responsibilities : Provides front line circulation service working in a team-based environment under the remote daily guidance of the Circulation Manager. Routine tasks include: Operating a web-based circulation system, providing reserve services, opening and closing the library building, assisting with training and supervising student assistants, shelving materials, and monitoring patron and building security during assigned hours. This position works consistent evening shifts (until 10pm) and Saturday shifts. Required Qualifications : High School Diploma or GED Foundational knowledge of Microsoft products such as Word, Excel, Outlook Minimum 1 year of library experience or direct customer service experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knows how to communicate and interact effectively with patrons and colleagues in person, electronically, and via the telephone to provide quality customer service. Knows how to operate and troubleshoot office equipment, including photocopiers and microform reader/printers, computers, printers in order to assist patrons and ensure they are working efficiently. Knows how to use Microsoft Word and Excel to maintain records and prepare reports. Knows how to use web editing software in order to create, modify, and publish web content. Knows how to use the integrated library system to circulate materials, prepare notices, place holds and/or recalls, conduct basic processing, and obtain statistical data. Ability to schedule, train, and supervise student assistants and evaluate their work to ensure effective workflow. Ability to move boxes and materials of up to 30 pounds in order to shelve and or move library materials with or without reasonable accommodation.  Ability to produce accurate work, ability to organize work, and ability to set and adjust priorities. Ability to push fully loaded book trucks, and ability to reach and bend to shelve library materials with or without reasonable accommodation.  Ability to use independent judgment to make appropriate decisions. Ability to work as part of a team and to work cooperatively and creatively with colleagues to maintain a positive work environment. Preferred Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree, or an equivalent combination of education and appropriate library work experience. Software: Alma / Ex-Libris (Library Management System) Experience, Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Up to one year of library experience, with preference for academic library experience. Experience using an integrated library system Experience with HTML or web content software, such as Plone. Demonstrated efficiency with Word and Excel. Experience troubleshooting basic computer technology problems. Supervisory experience.   Background Check Contingencies: - Criminal History   Document Attachments: - Resume - Cover letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5   Job Family: Staff Library Services Non-exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
    },
    "https://merceruniversity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/external/job/Macon-GA--31207/Front-Desk-Support-Specialist_27-152": {
      "title": "Front Desk Support Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nApplication Instructions: External Applicants: Please upload your resume on the Apply screen. Your application will automatically populate your resume details, and you may verify and update data on the My Information page.   IMPORTANT: Please review the job posting and load ALL documents required in the job posting to the Resume/CV document upload section at the bottom of the My Experience application page. Use the Select Files button to add multiple documents including your Resume/CV, references, cover letter, and any other supporting documents required in the job posting. The \" My Experience\" page is the only opportunity to add your required supporting document attachments. You will not be able to modify your application after you submit it .   Current Mercer University Employees : Apply from your existing Workday account. Do not apply from the external careers website . Log in to Workday and type Jobs Hub in the search bar. Locate the position and click Apply . Job Title: Front Desk Support Specialist   Department: Mercer Medicine   College/Division: School Of Medicine   Primary Job Posting Location: Macon, GA 31207 Additional Job Posting Locations: (Other locations that this position could be based) Job Details: The Mercer Medicine clinic in Macon, GA is searching for a Front Desk Support Specialist.   Responsibilities : The candidate in this position acts as a medical secretary/receptionist for the front desk at a multi-specialty practice. Handles check in and check out of patients, collects payments and posts charges/payments. Responsible for appointment scheduling, rescheduling, and cancellations. Responsible for appointment reminders, accurate data entry of all patient information, entering information into the EMR, updating of demographics, updating of pertinent information, scanning and copying records as required. This individual is responsible for handling multiple phone calls and creating a professional and welcoming environment for Mercer Medicine. Qualifications : A high school diploma or GED is required, along with one year of healthcare office experience to include hands on computer knowledge of electronic medical records, preferably EMD and/or Athena. The successful candidate must be able to provide excellent customer service with a professional, yet friendly, disposition. Must be flexible and adapt to change well. The ability to maintain composure and the awareness of when to seek help from supervisors are essential.   Background Check Contingencies : - Criminal History Check - Credit Check   Documents : - Resume - Cover Letter - List of three professional references with contact information   About Mercer University Founded in 1833, Mercer University is a distinguished private institution recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, leadership development, and community engagement. With campuses across Georgia, Mercer’s twelve schools and colleges offer a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The university cultivates a close-knit, student-centered environment where innovation, service, and personal growth are deeply valued. Mercer’s employees are at the heart of its mission, dedicated to advancing innovation, supporting student success, and strengthening both our local and global communities through service. At Mercer, we believe in the power of relationships and the importance of in-person collaboration. Accordingly, our employees are expected to serve in-person as it fosters real-time problem solving, mentoring, and the meaningful connections that strengthen both our work and service to our students and the broader university community.  Why Work at Mercer University Mercer University offers a variety of benefits for eligible employees including comprehensive health insurance (for self and dependents), generous retirement contributions , tuition waivers , paid vacation and sick leave , technology discounts, schedules that allow for work-life balance, and  so much more! At Mercer University, a Bear is more than a mascot: it's a frame of mind that begins with a strong desire to make the most out of your career. Mercer Bears do not settle for mediocrity or the status quo. If you're seeking an environment where your passion and determination are embraced, then you want to work at Mercer University.    For more information, please visit:  https://hr.mercer.edu/prospective-employees/ Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40   Job Family: Staff Clinical Services Non-exempt   EEO Statement: EEO/Veteran/Disability"
